oads multiple times with short backoff\n  - fall back to `nodes_template` only if needed\n  - treat bad “success” payloads like `{\"Error\":{}}`, missing `path`, or missing `filename` as real failures\n  - save:\n    - `upload-request.json`\n    - `upload-response.json`\n    - `upload-attempts.json`\n- In `SKILL.md` I aligned the instructions to the real working behavior:\n  - primary upload target is now `nodes_bucket`\n  - fallback is `nodes_template`\n  - manual multipart via stdlib is allowed when `requests` is unavailable\n  - retries/backoff and artifact saving are now documented\n\n**Important note**\n- I fixed the **client-side mismatch and robustness issues**.\n- I **cannot honestly guarantee** “no more issues whatsoever,” because the upload service itself is intermittently returning `{\"Error\":{}}` even for the correct multipart request shape. That part is server-side behavior, not just script behavior.\n\n**What it means**\n- The skill is now internally consistent.\n- Future runs will use the corrected upload path first, retry automatically, and leave better diagnostics when the remote endpoint flakes.\n\n**Next sensible step**\n- If you want, I can do one more pass and make the script save a timestamped artifact set per run instead of overwriting the same files, so debugging across multiple failures is even cleaner.","textSignature":"{\"v\":1,\"id\":\"msg_0e0656b03cf29aaf0169bd8da4910481919f89426c2bb2d62f\",\"phase\":\"final_answer\"}"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.4","usage":{"input":244,"output":582,"cacheRead":62336,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":63162,"cost":{"input":0.0006100000000000001,"output":0.00873,"cacheRead":0.015583999999999999,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.024923999999999998}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1774030236176}}
